   "text": "This drawing is esomeprazole magnesium: two (S)-omeprazole anions with one Mg\u00b2\u207a. I identified it as esomeprazole from the overall layout and the single hashed S\u2013CH\u2082 bond. The sulfur stereo-label comes from my recollection of the known (S)-omeprazole SMILES, re-ordered to match my atom order, not from deriving CIP priorities from the hash.\n\nReading each ligand from the drawing:\n- **Pyridine ring:** 4-methoxy-3,5-dimethylpyridine, linked through its C2 to a CH\u2082 group.\n- **Sulfinyl group:** CH\u2082 connects to a sulfoxide S(=O), which is drawn with a hashed bond and so is a stereocentre.\n- **Benzimidazole:** the S is attached at C2. One ring nitrogen is drawn as a neutral =N and the other as N\u207b. The methoxy sits on the benzo carbon para to the carbon bonded to N\u207b, so I wrote it as `COc1ccc2[n-]c(nc2c1)`.\n\nSMILES: [Mg+2].COc1ccc2[n-]c(nc2c1)[S@](=O)Cc1ncc(C)c(OC)c1C.COc1ccc2[n-]c(nc2c1)[S@](=O)Cc1ncc(C)c(OC)c1C"
